Link: https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/375/D
Brief summary: Count number of elements that occur >= k times in v's subtree
Comment: Can be solved using MO's algo, because of incrementing cnt[color] one by one we can keep track of prefix sums
But instead of MO's we can count something for every subtree by adding and deleting each subtree except the largest one
Something like:
dfs_solve(v):
  for i in childs[v]:
    if(i != max_child):
        dfs_solve(i)
        dfs_remove(i)
  dfs_solve(max_child)
  for i in childs[v]:
    if(i != max_child):
      dfs_add(i)
  add(v)

This works because by traversing edge that connects parent and non-max child size of tree doubles, so each vertex gets deleted at most logn times.
